description:
FILED s538a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-12) from the #3615 acceptance run: with `@_{@hdr}` fixed, Text-CSV t/91_csv_cb.t runs to its plan (77 ok of 79) and the two rows left are this.  PRE-EXISTING (main 23f0f917 emits the same).

REPRO (perl 5.40.3 vs PCL; scratch/s538a/pr/pctunder.pl in the s538a worktree):
    package Foo;
    sub f { my $cb = shift; local %_; $_{a} = 1; @_{qw(b c)} = (2, 3); return $cb->() }
    sub g { return join ",", map { "$_=$_{$_}" } sort keys %_ }
    sub h { local %_ = (z => 26); return main::peek() }
    package main;
    sub peek { return join ",", map { "$_=$_{$_}" } sort keys %_ }
    print "1 ", Foo::f(sub { join ",", map { "$_=$_{$_}" } sort keys %_ }), "\n";   # perl a=1,b=2,c=3   PCL (empty)
    %_ = (m => 13); print "2 ", Foo::g(), "\n";                                       # perl m=13          PCL (empty)
    print "3 ", Foo::h(), " after=", peek(), "\n";                                    # perl z=26 after=m=13   PCL m=13 after=m=13
    { package Bar; print "4 ", scalar(keys %_), "\n"; }                              # 1 both (a package BLOCK already reads main's)
`_` is a forced-main name (perl's gv_fetchpvn: `_` with any sigil lives in main::), and PCL's `+p-forced-main-names+` / `Pl::Environment::forced_main_names` list it -- but the `%_` VARIABLE in a package section is emitted as a bare `%_` interned in that package's CL package (`(p-defcell %_ ...)` per unit), not main's.  `$_` / `@_` reach main's because pcl EXPORTS them (ExprToCL's %PCL_EXPORTED_GLOBALS); `%_` is not there.

FIX SHAPE (not started): `%_` joins the exported / main-pinned globals the way `@_` / `$_` did -- read docs/DECIDED.md §s451z and the note above Parser2's %PKG_SWITCH_IMMUNE_VARS first: FOUR tables share that membership deliberately and Pl/t/global-partition-01.t pins the coincidence; the per-unit `(p-defcell %_ ...)` must then not rebind it.  BAR: the four rows above vs perl, Text-CSV 91_csv_cb.t rows 26 + 45 (one-file run), the sweep (a global-partition change).
